B.a7Y=s(["The **ovarian cycle** happens in the ovaries. An egg grows in a small sac called a follicle, then breaks free. This is _ovulation_.","The **uterine cycle** happens inside the uterus. Its lining thickens to hold a fertilised egg. When no egg arrives, the lining is shed and leaves the body as a period."],t.s)
B.a1Q=new A.aU("Two cycles at once",B.a7Y)
B.aeM=s(["Hormones run the whole process. The brain sends signals to the ovaries, which respond by releasing hormones of their own. Two of them, **FSH** and **LH**, do most of the work. A sharp rise in LH is what triggers ovulation.","If pregnancy happens, a hormone from the new embryo keeps the lining in place. Without it, hormone levels drop and the period starts."],t.s)
B.a0K=new A.aU("What controls it",B.aeM)
B.a52=s(["Cycle length changes from person to person, and month to month. !!The 28-day average is a midpoint, not a target.!!","Your cycle can shift with stress, illness, weight change, heavy exercise, breastfeeding or hormonal birth control. !!Irregular cycles are common in the first years after a first period and again later in life.!!"],t.s)
B.a0V=new A.aU("It is not a clock",B.a52)
B.ab4=s([B.a1Q,B.a0K,B.a0V],t.r)
B.YC=new A.cu("The menstrual cycle","What it is, how it is counted, and what controls it","The menstrual cycle is the monthly set of changes a body goes through before a pregnancy. It ends with a period when pregnancy does not happen. You count it **from the first day of one period to the first day of the next**.",B.a46,B.ab4)
B.a_l=new A.a7("Menstrual phase","About 3 to 7 days")
B.a_j=new A.a7("Follicular phase","About 7 to 14 days")
B.a_0=new A.a7("Ovulation lasts","24 to 36 hours")
B.a_S=new A.a7("Luteal phase","About 12 to 14 days")
B.a2Z=s([B.a_l,B.a_j,B.a_0,B.a_S],t.E)
B.a9W=s(["**Menstrual** is the period itself, when the uterine lining is shed.","**Follicular** starts on the same day your period begins, while a follicle grows and oestrogen rises. This phase is the most variable part of your cycle."],t.s)
B.a0C=new A.aU("Menstrual and follicular",B.a9W)
B.af3=s(["**Ovulation** is the release of the egg, roughly two weeks before your next period. !!It happens earlier or later than day 14 more often than people expect.!!","**Luteal** runs from ovulation until your next period. The leftover follicle, now called the corpus luteum, releases progesterone. This phase is remarkably consistent, near 12 to 14 days."],t.s)
B.a27=new A.aU("Ovulation and luteal",B.af3)
B.a4s=s(["Energy, mood and discharge all tend to follow these phases. Knowing where you are in the cycle can make a difficult week feel explainable rather than mysterious."],t.s)
B.a0O=new A.aU("Why the phases matter",B.a4s)
B.aaf=s([B.a0C,B.a27,B.a0O],t.r)
B.YK=new A.cu("The four phases","Menstrual, follicular, ovulation and luteal","A cycle has four phases. Two happen together at the start, then ovulation, then a short luteal phase before the next period. !!Almost all of the variation in cycle length comes from the follicular phase.!!",B.a2Z,B.aaf)
B.a_V=new A.a7("People who get PMS","About 8 in 10")
B.ZJ=new A.a7("People with PMDD","About 3 to 8 in 100")
B.a0o=new A.a7("How long cramps last","1 to 3 days")
B.ZG=new A.a7("Cramps are caused by","Prostaglandins")
B.a3y=s([B.a_V,B.ZJ,B.a0o,B.ZG],t.E)
B.acP=s(["**PMS** is the name for the cluster of symptoms that can appear in the week before a period: bloating, breast tenderness, headaches, tiredness, food cravings and mood swings.","!!PMS is very common and it is treatable.!! Symptoms that only ever show up in the luteal phase and ease once the period starts are a strong clue."],t.s)
B.a1M=new A.aU("PMS",B.acP)
B.afe=s(["**PMDD** is a more severe form, diagnosed when symptoms seriously affect work, school or relationships. Unlike PMS it can be disabling.","It is not a character flaw and not simply bad moods. It is a recognised condition with real treatments, including ones that help before a period starts."],t.s)
B.a1F=new A.aU("PMDD",B.afe)
B.a4Z=s(["Cramps come from **prostaglandins**, chemicals that make the uterus contract. They are strongest in the first days of bleeding and usually ease after that.","Heat, gentle movement and anti-inflammatory painkillers help most people. !!Pain that stops you getting on with your day is not something you should simply put up with.!!"],t.s)
B.a1v=new A.aU("Period pain",B.a4Z)
B.a5G=s([B.a1M,B.a1F,B.a1v],t.r)
B.YF=new A.cu("Symptoms and PMS","Common signs, PMS, PMDD and period pain","Most people notice some change around their period. Most symptoms are mild and pass. A smaller number get symptoms severe enough to disrupt daily life, which is worth treating.",B.a3y,B.a5G)
B.a_L=new A.a7("Sleep","7 to 9 hours a night")
B.a_z=new A.a7("Movement","Most days of the week")
B.ZH=new A.a7("Best for cramps","Heat and gentle movement")
B.a_3=new A.a7("Worth tracking","Flow, mood and pain")
B.acH=s([B.a_L,B.a_z,B.ZH,B.a_3],t.E)
B.ac8=s(["**Sleep and meals** matter most. Skipping meals tends to make cramps and cravings worse rather than easier.","**Movement** that suits your body is enough. There is no ideal cycle phase for exercise, so do what feels good and skip what does not."],t.s)
B.a24=new A.aU("Everyday basics",B.ac8)
B.a2I=s(["Heat on your lower abdomen, gentle stretching or a walk are reliable for cramps. Reduce caffeine if it clearly worsens your symptoms.","**Lower your expectations.** A week of low mood is temporary, and planning around it is more useful than fighting it."],t.s)
B.a1r=new A.aU("During a difficult week",B.a2I)
B.a6V=s(["Tracking flow, mood and pain over a few cycles makes patterns easier to see. !!What looks random in the moment is often obvious once it is written down.!!"],t.s)
B.a1I=new A.aU("Use your data",B.a6V)
B.a4I=s([B.a24,B.a1r,B.a1I],t.r)
B.YE=new A.cu("Looking after yourself","Small things that make a difficult cycle easier","You do not need a perfect routine. A few habits tend to help more than a long list of rules, and most of them cost nothing.",B.acH,B.a4I)
B.a_E=new A.a7("A missed period usually means","Pregnancy, until proven otherwise")
B.a_N=new A.a7("Tampons are linked to","Toxic shock, but rarely")
B.ZO=new A.a7("Very intense exercise can cause","A missed period, occasionally")
B.a0x=new A.a7("PMS compared with","PMDD, but milder")
B.a4K=s([B.a_E,B.a_N,B.ZO,B.a0x],t.E)
B.aah=s(["**You cannot get pregnant while breastfeeding.** Breastfeeding does reduce fertility, but not reliably enough to rely on on its own. !!Use contraception if you do not want to conceive.!!","**You must have a 28-day cycle.** Ranges from 21 to 35 days are normal in adults, and _your own average is more useful than any number from a textbook_."],t.s)
B.a1E=new A.aU("Two beliefs worth dropping",B.aah)
B.acr=s(["**You lose a lot of blood during a period.** The average is about 30 to 40 mL, closer to a few tablespoons than to what many people imagine. !!Soaking a pad every hour for several hours is worth mentioning to a doctor.!!","**Tampons are dangerous.** They are safe when changed on time. The serious infection linked to them is rare and linked to leaving one in far too long."],t.s)
B.a0R=new A.aU("Half-true",B.acr)
B.a45=s([B.a1E,B.a0R],t.r)
B.YW=new A.cu("Common myths","Things people often believe, and what is actually true","A lot of period advice is repeated until it sounds obvious. Here is what the evidence actually supports.",B.a4K,B.a45)
B.Z5=new A.a7("See a doctor if bleeding lasts","More than 7 days")
B.a_y=new A.a7("Also worth reporting","Bleeding between periods")
B.a_p=new A.a7("Get urgent help for","Sudden severe one-sided pain")
B.ZI=new A.a7("Help is warranted if symptoms","Stop you managing daily life")
B.a8P=s([B.Z5,B.a_y,B.a_p,B.ZI],t.E)
B.ab6=s(["Bleeding that lasts **longer than seven days**, or between periods, or after menopause.","Periods that become very heavy, very painful or suddenly irregular when they never used to be.","!!Symptoms that stop you working, studying or seeing people deserve to be taken seriously.!!"],t.s)
B.a1N=new A.aU("Book an appointment",B.ab6)
B.a2n=s(["**Sudden severe pain on one side of the lower belly**, especially with fainting, shoulder pain or bleeding. This can mean an ectopic pregnancy or a twisted ovarian cyst.","**Fever with pelvic pain or foul-smelling discharge**, which can mean an infection that needs antibiotics."],t.s)
B.a1e=new A.aU("Get urgent help",B.a2n)
B.acg=s([B.a1N,B.a1e],t.r)
B.YI=new A.cu("When to see a doctor","Symptoms that deserve a check-up","Most period problems are ordinary and treatable. A few signs are worth getting checked rather than waiting to see if they settle.",B.a8P,B.acg)
B.a0e=new A.a7("Usual age range","9 to 16")
B.ZD=new A.a7("Worth a check-up after age","15")
B.Zj=new A.a7("What the first flow looks like","Light spotting first")
B.a01=new A.a7("Cycles often settle within","2 to 3 years")
B.abD=s([B.a0e,B.ZD,B.Zj,B.a01],t.E)
B.a6p=s(["**Breast development and pubic hair** usually come first, often a year or two before the first period. Growth and height also change throughout, not all at once.","The first flow is often light spotting that darkens over a day or two rather than starting all at once."],t.s)
B.a0W=new A.aU("What happens first",B.a6p)
B.a7u=s(["For the first couple of years cycles are often long, short or unpredictable while hormones settle. !!One long gap is not on its own a sign that something is wrong.!!","It helps to know the signs of a period in advance, carry a product you are comfortable with, and know where a spare is kept. **Periods are not shameful** and you are allowed to ask about them anywhere."],t.s)
B.a23=new A.aU("Irregular at first",B.a7u)
B.a82=s([B.a0W,B.a23],t.r)
B.YG=new A.cu("Your first period","What to expect, and how to prepare","A first period usually arrives between ages 9 and 16. It arrives earlier for some and later for others, and !!a late first period is worth mentioning to a doctor after age 15.!!",B.abD,B.a82)
B.Zf=new A.a7("Condoms also protect against","Sexually transmitted infections")
B.a_s=new A.a7("Pregnancy rate with the pill","About 7 in 100 a year")
B.Zz=new A.a7("Pregnancy rate with a condom","About 13 in 100 a year")
B.Zs=new A.a7("Emergency pills work best within","72 hours")
B.abI=s([B.Zf,B.a_s,B.Zz,B.Zs],t.E)
B.a3v=s(["**Condoms** stop sperm reaching an egg and also reduce the risk of sexually transmitted infections. They are the only option that does both.","**The pill and the implant** use hormones to stop an egg being released. The **copper IUD** works without hormones. All of them are effective, and which suits you depends on your health and preferences."],t.s)
B.a25=new A.aU("The main options",B.a3v)
B.a8z=s(["Real-world failure rates are higher than perfect-use rates, usually because of missed pills or incorrect fitting. !!A missed dose or a broken condom is a good reason to ask about emergency contraception.!!","Emergency pills work best the sooner they are taken, and do not protect against an infection that has already been passed on."],t.s)
B.a1Y=new A.aU("Using them well",B.a8z)
B.a7b=s([B.a25,B.a1Y],t.r)
B.Yq=new A.cu("Birth control","The main options and how they work","Contraception prevents pregnancy. It does not protect against sexually transmitted infections, so some people use two methods.",B.abI,B.a7b)
B.Gi=new A.Y(B.iZ,[B.YC,B.YK,B.YF,B.YE,B.YW,B.YI,B.YG,B.Yq],t.pc)
